---
import { PRICE_LATER, PRICE_NOW, PRODUCT_NAME } from '../config';
import LegalPage from '../components/legal/LegalPage.astro';
import {
  CONFIRM, CONTACT_EMAIL, GOVERNING_LAW, LICENSOR, LICENSOR_COUNTRY, MACS_PER_LICENCE, POLAR_TERMS, REFUND_DAYS, TRIAL_DAYS, VENUE,
} from '../components/legal/legal';

const toc = [
  { id: 'scope', label: 'What these terms cover' },
  { id: 'product', label: 'What you get' },
  { id: 'trial', label: 'Free trial' },
  { id: 'buying', label: 'Buying and prices' },
  { id: 'delivery', label: 'Delivery' },
  { id: 'refunds', label: 'Refunds' },
  { id: 'use', label: 'Using the app' },
  { id: 'warranty', label: 'Warranty and liability' },
  { id: 'law', label: 'Governing law' },
  { id: 'changes', label: 'Changes and contact' },
];
---
<LegalPage
  title={`Terms of sale · ${PRODUCT_NAME}`}
  heading="Terms of sale"
  description={`The terms for trying and buying ${PRODUCT_NAME}: one payment, lifetime updates, a ${TRIAL_DAYS}-day free trial and a ${REFUND_DAYS}-day refund.`}
  ogTheme="light"
  toc={toc}
>
  <h2 id="scope">What these terms cover</h2>
  <p>
    These terms apply when you download, try or buy {PRODUCT_NAME}, a Git client for macOS made by {LICENSOR}, an individual developer based in {LICENSOR_COUNTRY} ("we", "us"). Your use of the app itself is governed by the <a href="/eula">End User Licence Agreement</a> (EULA).
    Our <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> explains what data is involved. By buying or using {PRODUCT_NAME} you accept these terms and the EULA.
  </p>

  <h2 id="product">What you get</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A licence to use {PRODUCT_NAME} on up to <strong>{MACS_PER_LICENCE} Macs</strong> that you own or control, at the same time.</li>
    <li><strong>Lifetime updates</strong>: every future version of {PRODUCT_NAME} at no extra cost, for as long as we publish it. No renewals and no paid upgrades.</li>
    <li>Email support at <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    {PRODUCT_NAME} is a desktop app. There's no {PRODUCT_NAME} account, no hosted service and no subscription.
    It needs macOS and the <code>git</code> command-line tool; current system requirements are on the <a href="/download">download page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="trial">Free trial</h2>
  <p>
    Every download includes a free {TRIAL_DAYS}-day trial with every feature. It starts the first time you open the app and needs no account and no
    payment details. Nothing is charged when it ends. After the trial you can keep browsing your repositories read-only; buying a licence
    unlocks everything again.
  </p>

  <h2 id="buying">Buying and prices</h2>
  <p>
    {PRODUCT_NAME} is sold through <strong>Polar</strong>, our merchant of record and authorized reseller. When you buy, your contract of sale is with
    Polar under the <a href={POLAR_TERMS}>Polar buyer terms</a>. Polar takes the payment, calculates and collects VAT or sales tax for your country,
    and issues your receipt or invoice. Polar's name may appear on your card statement.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Price:</strong> a single one-time payment in US dollars (USD). The launch price is <strong>US${PRICE_NOW}</strong>. It will later rise to <strong>US${PRICE_LATER}</strong> for new buyers. A price rise never affects a licence you already own.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Tax:</strong> prices on this site exclude tax. Checkout shows any VAT or sales tax before you pay.</li>
    <li><strong>Payment methods:</strong> the cards and wallets shown at Polar checkout.</li>
    <li><strong>Discounts:</strong> any discount or promotion states its conditions where it's offered.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="delivery">Delivery</h2>
  <p>
    {PRODUCT_NAME} is delivered digitally. Right after payment, Polar emails your licence key to the address you used at checkout, and you can also
    find it in the Polar customer portal. You download the app from our <a href="/download">download page</a> and activate it with the key.
    Nothing is shipped. If your key doesn't arrive within an hour, check spam, then see <a href="/licence">licence help</a> or email us.
  </p>

  <h2 id="refunds">Refunds</h2>
  <p>
    If {PRODUCT_NAME} isn't right for you, ask for a full refund within <strong>{REFUND_DAYS} days</strong> of purchase. No questions asked.
    The licence key is deactivated when the refund is issued. Details: <a href="/refunds">refund policy</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>EU and UK buyers:</strong> because the app is digital content delivered immediately, the statutory 14-day right of withdrawal can end
    once you activate your licence, where you agreed to that at checkout. Our {REFUND_DAYS}-day refund applies anyway and goes further.
  </p>

  <h2 id="use">Using the app</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your licence is personal. Don't share, resell or publish your licence key, or use it on more than {MACS_PER_LICENCE} Macs at once.</li>
    <li>Don't break or bypass the licence check, or redistribute the app. The full rules are in the <a href="/eula">EULA</a>.</li>
    <li>We may deactivate a key that's been refunded, charged back, shared publicly or obtained by fraud.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="warranty">Warranty and liability</h2>
  <p>
    {PRODUCT_NAME} changes Git repositories. It records every ref change so you can undo it, but software can fail. <strong>Keep backups and push important work to a remote.</strong>
  </p>
  <p>
    Apart from the refund above and any rights you have by law, {PRODUCT_NAME} is provided "as is", without warranties of any kind, express or implied,
    including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement. To the extent the law allows, we're not liable for lost data,
    lost profits or indirect, incidental or consequential damages, and our total liability is limited to what you paid for your licence.
  </p>
  <p>
    Nothing in these terms limits rights you have as a consumer that can't be waived under the law of the country you live in, or liability that
    can't be limited by law, such as for fraud or for death or personal injury caused by negligence.
  </p>

  <h2 id="law">Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by {GOVERNING_LAW}. <span class="legal-placeholder">{CONFIRM}</span> Disputes go to {VENUE}, <span class="legal-placeholder">{CONFIRM}</span> unless the consumer law of your country gives you the right to bring a claim where you live.
    Please email us first; most problems are quicker to fix than to argue about.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms. Changes apply to purchases made after we publish them and never take away a licence or lifetime updates you've
    already bought. Questions: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>, or see <a href="/contact">contact</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
